<title>INDIA: India president orders ban on non-banking funds.</title>
<headline>India president orders ban on non-banking funds.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-01-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian President Shankar Dayal Sharma on Friday issued an ordinance banning the acceptance of funds by unincorporated bodies with effect from April 1, 1997, the United News of India (UNI) said.</p>
<p>It said: &quot;If such bodies hold any deposits on this date, these shall be repaid within a period of two years or immediately after such deposits become due for repayment, whichever is earlier.&quot;</p>
<p>UNI said the ordinance also makes more stringent the provisions regulating the non-banking finance companies, but gave no details.</p>
</text>
